<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6657"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 10:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Continued <a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/59/314.html?1107919701"> <b>from here</b></a>.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6657-->
<!--Post: 6683--><!--Time: 1107961670-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6683"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 7:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry if this is a repeat, this was one of those &#39;slap myself silly&#39; thoughts last evening. <BR> <BR>IMO the isolated double letters is simple. <BR>Ligature = ties, binds = BTK &#39;signature&#39;  <BR> <BR>It&#39;s too easy to throw off the simple and dig for something with &#39;deeper&#39; meanings.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6683-->
<!--Post: 6684--><!--Time: 1107961882-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6684"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nancydrew<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nancydrew<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 7:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;the rooster crows&#34; <BR> <BR>Today is the Chinese New Year, 2005 is the year of the rooster.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6684-->
<!--Post: 6685--><!--Time: 1107961949-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6685"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 7:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->wonder if BTK, in his latest post: <BR>Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 8:32 pm:      <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR>tick tock goes the watch...when will &#40;i&#41;t strike again...maybe when the rooster crows? <BR> <BR> was inspired by this: <BR> <BR><a href="http://216.239.59.104/search?q=cache:YrqGo3d4EUUJ:www.spirit-net.ca/sermons/b-ad01su.html%2B%22%2Bwhen%2Bthe%2Brooster%2Bcrows%22%2B%2Bpoem%2B%2Bdeath&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://216.239.59.104/search?q=cache:YrqGo3d4EUUJ: www.spirit-net.ca/sermons/b-ad01su.html&#43;%22&#43;when&#43;t he&#43;rooster&#43;crows%22&#43;%2Bpoem&#43;%2Bdeath&amp;hl=en</a> <BR> <BR>A READING FROM MARK 13:24-37  <BR> <BR> &#34;Therefore keep watch because you do not know when the owner of <BR>   the house will come back--whether in the evening, or at midnight, <BR>   or when the rooster crows, or at dawn.  If he comes suddenly, do <BR>   not let him find you sleeping.  What I say to you, I say to <BR>   everyone: &#39;Watch!&#39;&#34; <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6685-->
<!--Post: 6686--><!--Time: 1107962108-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6686"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 7:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->or this one: <BR> <BR>Perhan&#39;s Dream <BR>After Emir Kusturica&#39;s Time of the Gypsies 1989 <BR> <BR>When the rooster crows  <BR>they will place a gold coin on each of his dead eyes <BR>the sun will set before the dance is done <BR>on the seventh day they will mourn him <BR>with trumpets and flirting for the last time <BR> <BR>Perhan&#39;s dream never ends  <BR>night after night the moon slips into his bed <BR>filling his head with unimaginable stories of chaos <BR>it is only when he wakes that Perhan stands on his own two feet <BR>and looks at himself flying across the highways <BR>humming a tiny gypsy song. <BR> <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6686-->
<!--Post: 6690--><!--Time: 1107963191-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6690"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 7:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->or this? is he using a folk song as inspiration again?: <BR><a href="http://216.239.59.104/search?q=cache:Ch7NBdEroD0J:mypcclinic.com/forums/archive/index.php/t-3889%2B%22%2Bwhen%2Bthe%2Brooster%2Bcrows%22%2B%2Bwichita&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://216.239.59.104/search?q=cache:Ch7NBdEroD0J: mypcclinic.com/forums/archive/index.php/t-3889&#43;%22 &#43;when&#43;the&#43;rooster&#43;crows%22&#43;%2Bwichita&amp;hl=en</a> <BR> <BR>One of the most memorable folk songs included these lyrics:  <BR> <BR>&#34;When the rooster crows at the break of dawn, look out your window and I&#39;ll be gone. You&#39;re the reason I&#39;m traveling on, _______________________.&#34; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6690-->
<!--Post: 6695--><!--Time: 1107966507-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6695"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 8:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good work!! <BR> <BR>I hope he is not traveling or moving on.  I really do hope that is not the case.  That could only mean we will never know who he is.   <BR>All of his recent actions, including turning in two driver&#39;s licenses and giving a slight profile of himself to police, could be one last attempt to call attention to himself to recreate his legacy one last time?   <BR> <BR>I am willing to believe that each of the things mentioned above were all based on FROM MARK 13:24-37.  Meaning probably that BTK&#39;s mention of the crowing rooster at dawn is based on it as well.  I don&#39;t see how someone could mentione Rooster crowing at dawn and watching without having known about that verse in Mark.   <BR> <BR>Thanks... <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6695-->
<!--Post: 6697--><!--Time: 1107966861-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6697"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 8:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->...tick tock goes the WATCH.. <BR>he says... <BR> <BR>OK. <BR> <BR>I did not realize watches go &#34;TICK TOCK&#34;.. watches not usually not loud enough to tick tock.   <BR> <BR>But...he says he is WATCHING.   <BR>&#39;tick tock goes the WATCH&#39;...is he saying he will only WATCH for so long.?? <BR> <BR>What is the significance of using the word WATCH in place of the word CLOCK when he says &#34;tick tock goes the.....&#34;   <BR>Should be &#39;tick tock goes the clock&#39;...instead he says &#39;tick tock goes the WATCH&#34;....is he saying he will only WATCH for so long? <BR> <BR>Just a thought to consider. <BR>I wonder if <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6697-->
